- **The sync, this fork's tenth upstream take, in the shape the founder chooses at P4 [inferred].**
  - **The pin.** `upstream/main` (DioxusLabs/blitz) reads `563d3db73` ("Resolve transforms through anonymous block boxes (#1549)", committed 2026-11-13T12:39:22Z).
  - **The counts.** The merge base is still `23b9b26a9`, and `git rev-list` counts 164 upstream commits not in HEAD. Of those 164, 36 are already in as cherry-picks: our branch carries 36 distinct `(cherry picked from commit …)` trailers, every one naming a commit of the range. **That leaves 128 to take or leave:**
    - the 21 left out at the last take (the first freight block below);
    - 107 new since that take's pin `e42ee1f25`, none of them a merge commit.
  - **What the 107 bring.** Among them are:
    - registry moves: Stylo 0.24 (`2288d67d3`, with selectors 0.43 and html5ever/markup5ever 0.40) and Parley 0.13 (`085114b3f`);
    - git pins: AnyRender at `abec906c…` (`e4c5bc906`, `7b72c22bd`, `a367c9ecb`, …, vello 0.12) and Taffy at `a3997d55…` (`752ed2e49`, `b4952e15f`);
    - DevTools/CDP (`d63145027` and the `CDP:` commits), `parley_code_editor` (`60c3baffd`), a Skia default renderer for the browser app (`74861e747`) and the WPT manifest runner (`946f7c461`);
    - engine fixes and paint features: text-shadow (`795cddd5d`), CSS masks (`a946a0a7b`), lossy page decoding (`9b9471f2f`), the AccessKit refresh (`be60597f6`), a default-font fallback (`3a146c669`), an empty alt as decorative (`e65ec76e1`), a text-input copy firing no input event (`f8f9a26f6`), and others;
    - `da271cde1`, "Fix needless_bool lints from clippy 1.100" (#1545).
  - **Upstream's manifest at `563d3db73`** names stylo 0.24.0 (registry), git Taffy, git AnyRender (8 crates), Dioxus `0.8.0-alpha.3`, winit `=0.31.0-beta.4`, parley 0.13 and vello 0.12. **Ours** names stylo 0.22.0, taffy 0.15, anyrender 0.14, parley 0.12, Dioxus 0.7.3, winit `=0.31.0-beta.3` and vello 0.11.

- **The take is a fork, decided at P4 [inferred].**
  - **Precedent.** The founder chose a cherry-pick with the pins unchanged at the last three syncs: «Десять коммитов (Рекомендую)» (2026-10-24), «Одиннадцать коммитов (Рекомендую)» (2026-10-27) and the 2026-11-01 take recorded in `escher-0.3.0/chunks/2026-11-01-upstream-sync-ui-graph/`.
  - **The binding rules.** "the workspace takes no git dependency — every crate a crates.io registry version" (CLAUDE.md Critical Warnings; `.claude/rules/security.md` §Dependencies), and the coupled pins.
  - **The shapes P3 measures**, each on its own trial worktree:
    - a cherry-pick onto the registry pins, taking the commits that build without git Taffy, git AnyRender or Dioxus 0.8;
    - that take plus the registry moves upstream now makes (Stylo 0.24, Parley 0.13, winit beta.4). These are registry versions, so they add no git dependency, but "pins unchanged" no longer holds. Whether they build without the git pins they arrived beside is P3's reading;
    - merging `563d3db73` whole, which reverses his git-dependency rule, so it is his fork;
    - taking nothing.
  - **The entry's hint says "merged".** Whether that word names the take or is one shape among the four is his call, not a reading.
  - Whatever is chosen, the pin stays the measured sha `563d3db73`. Commits upstream adds later go to the next sync, and moving the pin is the operator's call.

- **Conflicts are measured per shape at P3** (`git merge-tree`, then the trial). Every resolution keeps both sides' intent:
  - the changed set's contract;
  - the clock invariant;
  - the select model and its list;
  - the hit stops and the scrolled-box bounds;
  - the stable ids and the snapshot;
  - the range and keyboard models;
  - `inert`;
  - the accessibility state reads.

- **Every escher proof still passes after the take:**
  - `bash .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh fast` and `bash .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh doc`;
  - the stand checks in both layout modes;
  - the incremental/non-incremental oracle;
  - the **a11y leg** (`bash .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh a11y`);
  - the **dependency audit** (`bash .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh audit`);
  - the `embolden` witness;
  - fork CI green on the pushed commit, with every job settled.

- **Clippy red on the five newest shas, CI#43403526693 at `19596fd4b`, job `Clippy` = failure.** The runner's stable toolchain moved to rustc 1.100.0 (2026-11-09). Its clippy fires `needless_bool` (`-D warnings`) at three sites:
  - `packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:3223`;
  - `packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:410`;
  - `packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:426`.
  The other four reds read the same way: CI#43388911531 at `22e763982`, CI#43387577453 at `8630d9702`, CI#43386370417 at `a1cf8eb3a`, and CI#43385067916 at `f84ccd9f5` (completed/cancelled, red by Clippy). Every later job on HEAD's run reads `skipped`, the dependency audit included. Upstream's `da271cde1` fixes the same lint. Whether it is taken or ported, and whether it lands at exactly these three sites, is P3's reading against that run. The acceptance is the clippy leg green under the toolchain CI runs.

- **Boundary widenings [inferred]:** a take can bring new content readers or crossings, every document and remote pages included. Candidates are:
  - DevTools/CDP, which may open a socket or port (CLAUDE.md: "a new socket, port, IPC endpoint or credential path is a security-plan amendment first");
  - lossy page decoding;
  - new attribute reads (font `face`/`size`, `valign`, alt as decorative);
  - text-shadow and mask paint;
  - the AccessKit refresh;
  - new env reads.
  Each one the chosen shape carries is **listed for the operator at P4, never settled silently** (the directive above), and becomes a wrap amendment by his answer.

- **Pin movers among the 107: 36** (re-derived: each commit's `git show --name-only` matching `(^|/)Cargo\.(toml|lock)$`). They are:
  - Stylo to git 0.23, then registry 0.24 (`88160ec98`, `2288d67d3`);
  - AnyRender to git main through seven repins, vello 0.12 (`76c62f77f` … `a367c9ecb`, `e4c5bc906`);
  - Taffy to git main five times (`35cdfc859` … `b4952e15f`, rev `a3997d55…`);
  - Parley to main, then 0.13 (`79f46393d`, `085114b3f`);
  - rustls everywhere (`62715e975`);
  - the CDP server crate `blitz-vibey-cdp-server` and DevTools (`a1670ef1b`, `73ff15c0d`, `d63145027`, `5be96ed0e`);
  - `parley_code_editor` (`60c3baffd`);
  - the wpt manifest runner (`946f7c461`, `c27b4ca14`);
  - `js-framework-benchmark` (`242eb0670`);
  - and others.
  - Upstream's root manifest at `563d3db73` names git `taffy` (`DioxusLabs/taffy` rev `a3997d55…`), eight git AnyRender crates (rev `abec906c…`), Dioxus `0.8.0-alpha.3`, winit `=0.31.0-beta.4`, stylo `0.24.0`, parley `0.13` and vello `0.12`.
  - `cargo search` reads registry stylo 0.24.0, parley 0.13.0, vello 0.12.0, winit 0.31.0-beta.4, dioxus 0.8.0-alpha.3, taffy 0.15.1 and anyrender 0.14.0. There is no registry release of upstream's git Taffy or AnyRender revisions.

- **Shape A, the registry-only cherry-pick** (`trial-a`, HEAD + `da271cde1`).
